   "start_page": 1,
   "summary": "Ambassador Joseph C. Grew transmits Embassy Report No. 1673 surveying conditions in Japan during February 1941. The report highlights diplomatic friction with the United States regarding the Far Eastern crisis, Japanese southward expansion, and Japanese attacks on American mission and commercial properties in China, alongside Admiral Nomura's arrival in Washington. It also reviews Japan's mediation of the border dispute between French Indochina and Thailand, military operations in Honan and Kwangtung, economic discussions with the Netherlands East Indies, negotiations with the Soviet Union, and proceedings in the Imperial Diet concerning national mobilization and the Imperial Rule Assistance Association. Appended are lists of despatches and telegrams sent to the Department during February 1941.",
