   "start_page": 47,
   "summary": "Ambassador Joseph C. Grew transmits Despatch No. 5531 enclosing Report No. 1674 on conditions in Japan during March 1941. It covers American representations against anti-foreign agitation and violence, notably an assault on the French Commercial Attaché in Kobe, as well as the arrest and trial of American missionaries in Korea under shrine-worship and sedition laws. The report analyzes Japanese press reactions to the passage of the U.S. Lend-Lease Act and President Roosevelt's speeches, reports on Japanese amphibious raids along the Kwangtung coast, discusses modified Japanese demands in the resumed Batavia negotiations, and documents the conclusion of Japanese mediation resulting in French Indochina ceding territories to Thailand.",
   "title": "Despatch No. 5531: Report of Conditions in Japan During the Month of March 1941 (Report No. 1674)",
